 "exif_conclusion": "TACO polygons live in the EXIF-corrected (displayed) coordinate space, which equals the COCO width/height fields. cv2.imdecode -- the loader Ultralytics uses -- applies EXIF and reproduces exactly those dimensions, so normalising polygons by COCO width/height is correct. Any loader that IGNORES EXIF (PIL Image.size based scaling, cv2.IMREAD_IGNORE_ORIENTATION) silently rotates masks by 90 or 180 degrees. Verified visually on batch_1/000104.JPG.",
